],"best_idea":"A third-person camera pulled in by walls with a fast pull-in and a slow give-back, a zoom debt repaid only after a clear spell, and a small yaw step-around before pulling in.","decision":"adapt","decision_why":"The donor pivot is centred on the character, not over the shoulder, so Frankendom keeps the collision and smoothing shape and adds a lateral shoulder offset to the pivot; the 88 degree pitch clamp is too loose for a follow camera and is not copied. Licence is restricted, so clean-room shape only.","decision_status":"proposed","acceptance":"A player backs into a wall in a zone: the camera slides in within about 0.1 s, does not jitter on a slope, eases back out over about 0.4 s once clear, and a client test asserts the rendered camera distance is never past the wall limit after the pull-in."}
